{"name":"New Limerick","hex":"#9dc209","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"new","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Newar."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Recently made, or created.","Of recent origin; having taken place recently."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/new"},{"term":"limerick","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A humorous, often bawdy verse of five anapaestic lines, with the rhyme scheme aabba, and typically having an 8–8–5–5–8 cadence."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/limerick"}],"entries":[{"title":"New Limerick, Maine","blocks":[{"text":"New Limerick is a town in Aroostook County, Maine, United States. The population was 574 at the 2020 census. The town was settled in 1775 and incorporated on March 18, 1837, from New Limerick Plantation. It received its name from the fact that many of its settlers had previously lived in Limerick in York County at the southern end of the state, which in turn was probably named after the Irish city of Limerick."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Aroostook_County_Maine_incorporated_and_unincorporated_areas_New_Limerick_highlighted.svg/330px-Aroostook_County_Maine_incorporated_and_unincorporated_areas_New_Limerick_highlighted.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Limerick%2C_Maine","wikidata":"Q3449541"},{"title":"Limerick","blocks":[{"text":"Limerick is a city in western Ireland, in County Limerick. It is in the province of Munster and is in the Mid-West which comprises part of the Southern Region. With a population of 102,287 at the 2022 census, Limerick is the third-most populous urban area in Ireland, and the fourth-most populous city on the island of Ireland. It was founded by Scandinavian settlers in 812, during the Viking Age."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/co